WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Hello 5B! Today's recorded lesson is about equivalent fractions.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Equivalent fractions show the same amount in different ways.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Imagine a pizza cut into 2 slices. You eat 1 of the 2 pieces.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Now cut the same pizza into 4 slices and eat 2. It's the same amount.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
So one half equals two quarters, and that equals four eighths.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The pieces get smaller, but there are more of them.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Here's the rule: multiply the top and the bottom by the same number.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
One half times two over two gives two quarters.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Let's check: is three sixths equal to one half?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Three times two is six, so yes, three sixths is one half.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Great work! Try the worksheet next to practise.
